      "bottomRightY": 169,
      "content": "Figure 6-17 shows the eye mask used for all eye diagram measurements. Referring to the figure, the time is measured from the crossing points of Txp/Txn. The time is called the eye width, and the voltage is the eye height. The eye height is to be measured at the maximum opening (at the center of the eye width ± 0.05 UI). Specific eye mask requirements are defined in Table 6-20.",
